MFQ binds to site M of Cx43 GJC
Our functional and structural data on MFQ and 2APB suggest that site M likely serves as the primary site for inhibitor action in Cx32 GJC. To determine whether site M is a universal inhibitory drug binding pocket in connexins, we analyzed the effects of MFQ on Cx43 using cryo-EM (
Fig 5A–5C
) and functional analysis in cell-based activity assays (
Fig 5D
).
